title: fpl-league-bot — one tick

note:
**At 09:00 and 21:00**, one Lambda wakes up, reads the live FPL state and works
out whether anything is due. Nothing is scheduled against the calendar:
gameweek deadlines move, and only 21 of 37 gaps in the season are actually 7
days apart.

The interval only bounds _how late_ a message can be — never when it is sent.
Those hours are chosen because that is when the digest gets pasted into the
group.


Scheduler -> Tick: invoke — `cron(0 9,21 * * ? *)` _(Europe/London)_

Tick -> FPL: GET `/bootstrap-static/`
FPL --> Tick: 38 events — `deadline_time`, `is_next`, `data_checked`

Tick -> FPL: GET `/leagues-classic/1058423/standings/`
FPL --> Tick: `league`, `standings.results[]`, `new_entries[]`

note: No auth on either call. Private league standings are readable by ID — membership is never checked.


group: Deadline reminder

if: next deadline is within `REMINDER_LEAD_HOURS`

Tick -> DDB: PutItem `SENT#GW#nn#REMINDER`\n_condition_ `attribute_not_exists(pk)`
DDB --> Tick: claimed

Tick -> Discord: POST webhook — raw body, `SUPPRESS_EMBEDS`
Discord -->> Phone: **⏰ FPL deadline — Gameweek 1**\n_Friday 21 Aug, 18:30 (1 day away)_

else: already claimed, or deadline too far out

DDB --> Tick: `ConditionalCheckFailedException`
note: This is the common branch — most ticks have nothing due. A 48h lead is wider than the 12h tick interval, so the window always catches a tick; the reminder lands 36–48h out and is sent exactly once.

end
end


group: Weekly digest

if: latest event has `data_checked == true`

note:
There is **no gameweek-end timestamp** in the API. `finished` means the
fixtures were played; `data_checked` means bonus points are applied and scores
are final. Triggering on `finished` would post pre-bonus totals.


Tick -> DDB: PutItem `SENT#GW#nn#DIGEST` _(conditional)_
DDB --> Tick: claimed

Tick -> DDB: Query latest `SNAPSHOT#GW#` < nn
DDB --> Tick: last week's table

Tick -> Tick: compute climbers / fallers\n_falls back to FPL_ `last_rank` _if no snapshot_

Tick -> Discord: POST webhook _(split at 2000 chars)_
Discord -->> Phone: **Table**, top 5 climbers, top 5 fallers,\ngameweek winner, wooden spoon, who just joined

Tick -> DDB: PutItem `SNAPSHOT#GW#nn`
note: Written **only after** a successful send, so a failed week never becomes next week's baseline.

else: league has not started

note: Pre-season `standings.results` is empty and every manager sits in `new_entries`. No table, so nothing is sent.

end
end


if: send fails

Tick -> DDB: DeleteItem — release the claim
note: Without this the message is lost forever: the marker would say "sent" and no later tick would retry.

Tick --> Scheduler: error → CloudWatch alarm

end


Phone -> WhatsApp: **manual copy-paste**

note:
The body is posted **raw**, carrying its WhatsApp markup. Copy it out with the
message menu's **Copy Text** — that returns the raw source, so `*bold*` still
pastes as bold here. Dragging a selection copies Discord's rendered text and
loses the markup.

The hop is manual because the WhatsApp Cloud API is business-to-individual
only: there is **no group-messaging endpoint**, at any tier.
